 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "В поисках критика  (In Search of the Critic)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "kostya": "Костя",
  "max": "Макс"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The critic could be anyone in the room. Kostya and Max stand at the bar and size up the guests, one table at a time. Have a listen first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Макс, смотри внимательно на зал!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Кто же из них может быть критиком?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Эти двое работают в соседнем банке.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, они наши постоянные гости.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "А тот мужчина у окна?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Он заказал рыбу и красное вино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Нет, настоящий критик такого не закажет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "А парень за столиком номер три?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Он слишком молод для ресторанного критика.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Критики обычно сидят в одиночестве.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "И записывают всё в блокнот.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Смотри, женщина за седьмым столиком!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Она очень строго смотрит на меню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Кажется, мы нашли нашего критика!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's slow it down.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Макс, смотри внимательно на зал!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Max, look carefully at the dining room!' Now we can analyze the speech: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "смотри",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a command to one friend, the familiar form of 'to look'. Then ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "на",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "зал",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " points that look at the room, with the preposition for 'at'. Kostya speaks in a conspirator's voice.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Кто же из них может быть критиком?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Which one of them could be the critic?' The expression is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Кто",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "же",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "из",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "них",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'who then of them', and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "может",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "быть",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'can be'. After 'be', the noun for critic gets a new ending, becoming ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "критиком",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Эти двое работают в соседнем банке.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Those two work at the bank next door.' Two people here are called ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "двое",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the term you use for a pair of people. After the preposition, the bank takes an ending, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "соседнем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'neighbouring', grows from the noun for 'neighbour'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, они наши постоянные гости.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, they are our regular guests.' You call regulars ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "постоянные",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "гости",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'constant guests'. Max agrees with Kostya's logic: regulars cannot be mystery visitors.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "А тот мужчина у окна?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And that man by the window?' Let's focus on the words: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "у",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "окна",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'at the window': after the preposition, the window takes a new ending. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "мужчина",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'man', is close to the noun for 'husband'. Kostya moves on to the next suspect.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Он заказал рыбу и красное вино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He ordered fish and red wine.' Listen to the fish: it turns into ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "рыбу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " because it's the thing he ordered. And ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "красное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " takes a matching ending for 'wine'. Max reads the table like a detective.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Нет, настоящий критик такого не закажет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, a real critic will not order that.' We can inspect the phrase: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "такого",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "закажет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'of such not will order', with the term for 'such' changed after 'not'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "закажет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'will order'. Kostya is sure of his rules for critics.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "А парень за столиком номер три?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What about the guy at table number three?' The opening word means 'and what about'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "за",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "столиком",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'at the little table': the noun is a small version of the usual word for a restaurant table.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Он слишком молод для ресторанного критика.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He is too young for a restaurant critic.' We can analyze the dialogue: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "молод",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a short form of 'young', used to describe someone in the moment. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "для",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "ресторанного",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "критика",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'for a restaurant critic', with new endings.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Критики обычно сидят в одиночестве.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Critics usually sit in solitude.' It sounds grand, but ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "одиночестве",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is just the usual way to say someone sits alone, and it's built on the term for 'one'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "обычно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'usually', comes first, as a general rule.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "И записывают всё в блокнот.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And write down everything in a notepad.' Now let's inspect the words: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "записывают",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'write down', using a prefix on the verb 'to write'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "блокнот",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'notepad', was borrowed from French. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "блокнот",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'into the notepad'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Смотри, женщина за седьмым столиком!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Look, the woman at table seven!' The table is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "за",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "седьмым",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "столиком",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'at the seventh little table', using a counting word. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "женщина",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'woman'. The suspect is a lady alone, so she fits.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Она очень строго смотрит на меню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She is looking very strictly at the menu.' We will look at the phrase: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "строго",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'strictly', takes an adverb ending. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "меню",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " never changes its ending here. Kostya is drawing a conclusion from a frown, which is hardly proof.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Кажется, мы нашли нашего критика!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It seems we found our critic!' Now we can break down this line: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Кажется",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'it seems', is a single word. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "нашли",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'found', ends in a plural suffix for 'we'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "нашего",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "критика",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'our critic' as the one found. Now let's hear it once more, start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
